583
01:05:05,940 --> 01:05:10,340
Now, as you can see, the guy on the tightrope, he's balancing quite nicely.

584
01:05:10,540 --> 01:05:18,840
And the basic illustration is that when the market is in balance, there tends to be a lot of control, a lot of two-way trade being facilitated.

585
01:05:19,040 --> 01:05:27,140
However, if all of a sudden things become shaky on the tightrope, then we start to see a little bit of panic, a little bit of volatility, a little bit of range expansion.

586
01:05:27,340 --> 01:05:33,940
And that is why we want to differentiate between a market that is in balance and a market that is out of balance.

587
01:05:34,340 --> 01:05:40,640
So, as we can see, a market that is in balance, it opens within the previous day's value area.

588
01:05:40,640 --> 01:05:53,940
So, where the market accepted prices the previous day, where buyers and sellers said, we are happy to agree as this being the fairest price on the day, if we open in and around that fair value, the market is said to be in balance.

589
01:05:53,900 --> 01:05:58,800
Now remember, when we're in balance, the market is said to be in firm control.

590
01:05:59,700 --> 01:06:06,400
Now remember, when we are in balance, there's a lower risk and therefore less opportunity.

591
01:06:06,400 --> 01:06:13,500
So what we mean by that is that there's a 50-50 chance when we're in balance that the market goes up or that it goes down.

592
01:06:13,500 --> 01:06:21,800
So again, there's slightly less opportunity or slightly less conviction in terms of the market either going up or going down.

593
01:06:21,800 --> 01:06:30,000
So crucial you understand that because again it brings us back to that concept of do we want to be aggressive when the market is not showing?

594
01:06:21,840 --> 01:06:32,540
So crucial you understand that because again it brings us back to that concept of do we want to be aggressive when the market is not showing that sort of aggressiveness.

595
01:06:30,700 --> 01:06:32,000
that sort of aggressiveness.

596
01:06:33,300 --> 01:06:36,600
Now, more time is spent when we are in balance.

597
01:06:36,800 --> 01:06:41,600
We do tend to spend a lot of time trading within the previous day's value.

598
01:06:41,600 --> 01:06:46,200
So it's almost like the market says, you know, we accepted these prices the day before.

599
01:06:46,400 --> 01:06:53,800
There's a higher probability we're going to initially accept these prices again today whilst we await further information.

600
01:06:54,400 --> 01:06:58,000
Now, the opposite to that is where a market opens out of balance.

601
01:06:58,000 --> 01:07:07,200
Now, when we open out of balance, we're opening outside of the value area or the accepted area of the previous day.

602
01:07:07,200 --> 01:07:16,000
So we almost get this idea where the market said previously the day before we accepted these prices and now today we're going to open

603
01:07:16,600 --> 01:07:26,100
lower or higher than where we accepted and then we're going to decide do we re-enter the previous day's accepted area, do we accept a new area today.

604
01:07:26,300 --> 01:07:39,300
